  "sign_convention_finding": {
    "id": "F-LIVE-02",
    "what": "`originated_spread` is documented and labelled as the HOME team's spread (negative = home favourite). The S2_SpreadValue selections emitted by nba2/picks.py apply the away-side sign to the team that is actually the favourite, producing labels such as 'POR +6.0' when POR is the favourite by 6.07 points (line label in the same file reads 'POR -6.0').",
    "evidence": "nba2/picks.py S2 branch: sel = f\"{away} {-originated_spread:+.1f}\" for margin<0",
    "consequence": "a reader of picks.json could take the wrong side of the model's own number; the grader here reproduces the committed selections exactly so the measurement is of what was published, not of what was intended",
